  "solution": {
    "text": "Let \\(u\\) be the initial velocity.\n\\(\\therefore v_{1}=u+a t_{1}, v_{2}=u+d\\left(t_{3}+t_{2}\\right) \\mathrm{and}\\)\n\\(v_{3}=u+a\\left(t_{1}+t_{3}+t_{3}\\right)\\)\nNow, \\(v_{1}=\\frac{u w_{1}}{2}, \\frac{u\\left(u+a t_{1}\\right)}{2}=u+\\frac{1}{2}\\) at,\n\\(v_{1}=\\frac{v_{1}+c_{2}}{2}+u+a t_{1}+\\frac{1}{2} a t_{2}\\)\n\\(v_{3}=\\frac{v_{2}+v_{2}}{2}=u+a t_{1}+a t_{2}+\\frac{1}{2} a t_{3}\\)\nSo, \\(\\left(y_{1}-v_{2}\\right)=-\\frac{1}{2} a\\left(t_{3}+t_{2}\\right)\\)\nand \\(\\left(v_{2}-v_{3}\\right)=-\\frac{1}{2}\\) a \\(\\left(t_{2}+t_{3}\\right)\\)\n\\(\\therefore \\frac{\\left(v_{1}-v_{2}\\right)}{\\left(v_{2}-v_{3}\\right)}=\\frac{\\left(t_{1}+t_{2}\\right)}{\\left(t_{2}+t_{3}\\right)}\\)",
